# ==================================================================
#  Kitsu API: GET requests to explore with the VS Code REST Client
# ==================================================================
#  How to use:
#   1. Install the "REST Client" extension in VS Code.
#   2. Click "Send Request" above any request.
#   3. Read the response: status code, headers, and body.
#
#  Requests are separated by ###
#  Kitsu docs: https://kitsu.docs.apiary.io/
# ==================================================================

@base = https://kitsu.app/api/edge


# ==================================================================
#  PART 1: Headers
#  Kitsu speaks JSON:API, so its format is application/vnd.api+json
# ==================================================================

### 1.1 The correct Accept header (this is what our app sends)
GET {{base}}/anime
Accept: application/vnd.api+json


### 1.2 No Accept header at all
#   Still 200! The server uses its default format.
#   Look at the Content-Type header in the response.
GET {{base}}/anime


### 1.3 The WRONG Accept header
#   We ask for plain JSON, but Kitsu only gives JSON:API.
#   Result: 406 Not Acceptable
GET {{base}}/anime
Accept: application/json


# ==================================================================
#  PART 2: Pagination
#  Kitsu sends 10 items per page by default, and 20 at most.
#  Look at "meta.count" (total items) and "links.next" (next page).
# ==================================================================

### 2.1 First page (items 1 to 10)
GET {{base}}/anime
Accept: application/vnd.api+json


### 2.2 Second page: skip the first 10 (this is what our scroll does)
GET {{base}}/anime?page[offset]=10
Accept: application/vnd.api+json


### 2.3 Bigger pages: 20 items per page (the maximum)
GET {{base}}/anime?page[limit]=20&page[offset]=0
Accept: application/vnd.api+json


### 2.4 More than the maximum
#   Result: 400 "Limit exceeds maximum page size of 20."
GET {{base}}/anime?page[limit]=25
Accept: application/vnd.api+json


# ==================================================================
#  PART 3: Ask only for the data you need (sparse fieldsets)
#  Each anime has more than 30 attributes, but our app uses 4.
#  fields[anime]=... tells the server which ones to send.
# ==================================================================

### 3.1 Everything (about 60 KB for 10 anime)
GET {{base}}/anime
Accept: application/vnd.api+json


### 3.2 Only the 4 fields our app uses (about 15 KB: 4x smaller!)
GET {{base}}/anime?fields[anime]=slug,description,averageRating,posterImage
Accept: application/vnd.api+json


### 3.3 Only the title and the rating
GET {{base}}/anime?fields[anime]=canonicalTitle,averageRating
Accept: application/vnd.api+json


# ==================================================================
#  PART 4: Sorting
#  sort=field    → ascending  (small to big)
#  sort=-field   → descending (big to small), note the minus sign
# ==================================================================

### 4.1 Highest rated first
GET {{base}}/anime?sort=-averageRating&fields[anime]=canonicalTitle,averageRating
Accept: application/vnd.api+json


### 4.2 Most popular first (rank 1 is the most popular)
GET {{base}}/anime?sort=popularityRank&fields[anime]=canonicalTitle,popularityRank
Accept: application/vnd.api+json


### 4.3 Newest first
GET {{base}}/anime?sort=-startDate&fields[anime]=canonicalTitle,startDate
Accept: application/vnd.api+json


# ==================================================================
#  PART 5: Filtering
#  filter[name]=value  → only items that match
#  Look at "meta.count": how many items matched?
# ==================================================================

### 5.1 Search by text
GET {{base}}/anime?filter[text]=naruto&fields[anime]=canonicalTitle
Accept: application/vnd.api+json


### 5.2 Exact match by slug
GET {{base}}/anime?filter[slug]=cowboy-bebop
Accept: application/vnd.api+json


### 5.3 By type: TV, movie, OVA, ONA, special, music
GET {{base}}/anime?filter[subtype]=movie&fields[anime]=canonicalTitle,subtype
Accept: application/vnd.api+json


### 5.4 By status: current (airing now), finished, upcoming
GET {{base}}/anime?filter[status]=current&fields[anime]=canonicalTitle,status
Accept: application/vnd.api+json


### 5.5 By age rating: G, PG, R
GET {{base}}/anime?filter[ageRating]=G&fields[anime]=canonicalTitle,ageRating
Accept: application/vnd.api+json


### 5.6 By year
GET {{base}}/anime?filter[seasonYear]=2020&fields[anime]=canonicalTitle,startDate
Accept: application/vnd.api+json


### 5.7 By category
GET {{base}}/anime?filter[categories]=adventure&fields[anime]=canonicalTitle
Accept: application/vnd.api+json


### 5.8 Put it all together: best TV anime of 2020, 5 per page
#   A long query can be split over several lines (start with ? then &)
GET {{base}}/anime
    ?filter[seasonYear]=2020
    &filter[subtype]=TV
    &sort=-averageRating
    &page[limit]=5
    &fields[anime]=canonicalTitle,averageRating,startDate
Accept: application/vnd.api+json


# ==================================================================
#  PART 6: One anime by id
#  The URL has an id at the end, and "data" is an OBJECT, not a list
# ==================================================================

### 6.1 One anime
GET {{base}}/anime/1
Accept: application/vnd.api+json


### 6.2 One anime, only some fields
GET {{base}}/anime/1?fields[anime]=canonicalTitle,synopsis,episodeCount
Accept: application/vnd.api+json


### 6.3 An id that does not exist
#   Result: 404 "Record not found"
GET {{base}}/anime/999999999
Accept: application/vnd.api+json


# ==================================================================
#  PART 7: Related data
#  An anime is connected to other resources: episodes, categories...
#  Look at "relationships" in the response of 6.1
# ==================================================================

### 7.1 The episodes of an anime
GET {{base}}/anime/1/episodes?fields[episodes]=number,canonicalTitle
Accept: application/vnd.api+json


### 7.2 The categories of an anime
GET {{base}}/anime/1/categories?fields[categories]=title
Accept: application/vnd.api+json


### 7.3 The anime AND its categories in ONE request
#   include=... adds the related items in "included" at the end of the response
GET {{base}}/anime/1?include=categories&fields[categories]=title
Accept: application/vnd.api+json


# ==================================================================
#  PART 8: Other endpoints
# ==================================================================

### 8.1 Trending anime this week
GET {{base}}/trending/anime
Accept: application/vnd.api+json


### 8.2 All categories, the biggest first
GET {{base}}/categories?sort=-totalMediaCount&fields[categories]=title,totalMediaCount
Accept: application/vnd.api+json


# ==================================================================
#  PART 9: Errors
#  Read the status code AND the "errors" array in the body:
#  a real API tells you exactly what you did wrong.
# ==================================================================

### 9.1 A path that does not exist → 404
GET {{base}}/animee
Accept: application/vnd.api+json


### 9.2 A filter that does not exist → 400 "Filter not allowed"
GET {{base}}/anime?filter[banana]=1
Accept: application/vnd.api+json


### 9.3 A sort that does not exist → 400 "Invalid sort criteria"
GET {{base}}/anime?sort=banana
Accept: application/vnd.api+json


### 9.4 The old domain. Kitsu moved from kitsu.io to kitsu.app.
#   It still answers today, but real APIs move: always use the address in the docs.
GET https://kitsu.io/api/edge/anime
Accept: application/vnd.api+json


# ==================================================================
#  PART 10: Real data is not perfect (keep this in mind!)
#  A real API can send null for a value you expected to always exist.
# ==================================================================

### 10.1 Upcoming anime: nobody has rated them yet
#   Look at "averageRating" in each item. What is its value?
#   What would Anime.fromJson do with it?
GET {{base}}/anime?filter[status]=upcoming&fields[anime]=slug,description,averageRating,posterImage
Accept: application/vnd.api+json
